spec: specs/optics.md, the filed lane

why: the operator's call (2026-09-10). The spec filed this lane "by a
  consumer that needs it; none does" — the operator asked for it
  anyway, and the concern is noted rather than re-argued. What makes
  it more than an optimisation: the CONCRETE representation is itself
  a profunctor, so compiling an optic is instantiating it there — the
  existential-to-profunctor isomorphism of chapter 10, executed once
  instead of on every call.

what: `Optic.Market` (a Strong AND Choice profunctor whose carrier is
  the pair `(S => Either[T, A], (S, B) => T)`) and `o.compiled`, which
  runs the optic at it once and answers a concrete affine with direct
  `preview`/`set`/`modify`; the Bazaar (a Walk as a Traversing
  profunctor) for traversals if the first measurement earns it. Laws:
  a compiled optic answers what the optic answers, on every family and
  every operation. JMH: the composed `set` the 3.5x was measured on.

predict: the win is real for a composed optic and nil for a single
  lens (there is no chain to pay). If the compiled traversal is not
  faster than `Function1`'s direct road, it does not ship.
